# Qwen3.6-27B-FP8 — SINGLE-STREAM fusion lever: THREAD attn_metadata into the GDN (Angle B).
# =================================================================================================
# WHY (the lever): the champion runs EAGER (PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=0 + torch.compile, REGIONAL = each
#   decoder layer is its own torch.compile region). The GatedDeltaNet forward reads its metadata via
#   get_forward_context() (models/qwen3_5.py HPUGatedDeltaNetAttention._extract_metadata) — a dynamo
#   graph-break. With the break INSIDE the GDN (after input_layernorm), every linear-attention layer
#   compiles as TWO graphs: [input_layernorm] + [GDN scan/conv + norm + out_proj + MLP]. On-card
#   step-timer (SS bs=1): exec_med ~31ms / gap ~0.3ms => device-exec / op-dispatch bound.
#
# THE FIX (QWEN_GDN_THREAD_META=1, default-off/byte-identical): fetch attn_metadata ONCE at the TOP
#   of the decoder layer (above input_layernorm, in the EAGER model-forward-driven layer body) and
#   thread it into the GDN as an explicit ARG. dynamo then sees a graph INPUT instead of a contextvar
#   read, so the GDN break disappears and the WHOLE decoder-layer body fuses into ONE graph (mirrors
#   how the full-attention path already avoids the break via the unified-attention custom op, and how
#   HPUAttentionImpl.forward takes attn_metadata as an arg). Fewer/larger device kernels -> lower exec.
#   Same metadata object, same ops, same order -> behaviour-preserving by construction; on-card
#   coherence + step-timer is the arbiter.
#
# REQUIRES the patched _src plugin mounted (EXTRA_MOUNTS below) — the fix lives in
#   _src/vllm_gaudi/models/qwen3_5.py (GDN accepts a threaded attn_metadata arg + a gated, structurally
#   guarded reproduction of Qwen3NextDecoderLayer.forward that fetches meta at the layer top). The
#   guard falls back to the stock get_forward_context path + warns LOUD if upstream forward diverged.
#
# GATES (run in order): 1) serve up, look for the "[QWEN_GDN_THREAD_META=1] Installed threaded-metadata
#   Qwen3NextDecoderLayer.forward" log (if you see the "does not match ... NOT installing" warning, the
#   mounted vllm's decoder forward diverged from the reproduction -> re-sync the patch). 2) greedy
#   COHERENCE (Paris / 144 / first 10 primes) — watch the fp8<->bf16-GDN boundary. 3) step-timer:
#   exec_med must DROP from ~31ms. 4) SS c1 tok/s vs eager base ~32-33 (dynshapes-off base ~39).
#
# STACKS WITH dynshapes-off: for the fastest SS, also add `-e VLLM_T_COMPILE_DYNAMIC_SHAPES=false`
#   (the +18% SS lever; concurrency-jittery — SS-only). Test the fusion lever alone FIRST for a clean A/B.
#
# DEFAULT-SAFE: without QWEN_GDN_THREAD_META the plugin is byte-identical to stock. This env is opt-in.
# =================================================================================================
IMAGE=vllm-gaudi:next
MODEL_PATH=Qwen3.6-27B-FP8
SERVED_NAME=qwen36-27b
# Mount the patched dev plugin over the in-image one (carries the gated QWEN_GDN_THREAD_META fix).
EXTRA_MOUNTS="-v $HOME/AI/_src/vllm_gaudi:/opt/vllm-gaudi/vllm_gaudi"
# EAGER (the proven Qwen3.6 path) + QWEN_GDN_THREAD_META=1 (the fusion lever). Everything else = base.
MODEL_ENV="-e PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=0 -e PT_HPU_WEIGHT_SHARING=0 -e QWEN_GDN_THREAD_META=1 -e VLLM_SKIP_WARMUP=true -e VLLM_ENGINE_ITERATION_TIMEOUT_S=1800 -e VLLM_RPC_TIMEOUT=100000000 -e VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600 -e VLLM_DECODE_BS_BUCKET_MIN=1 -e VLLM_GRAPH_RESERVED_MEM=0.10 -e VLLM_HPU_LOG_STEP_CPU_FALLBACKS=true"
VLLM_ARGS="--quantization fp8 --kv-cache-dtype fp8_inc --tensor-parallel-size 8 --max-model-len 2048 --max-num-seqs 64 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.04 --block-size 128 --async-scheduling --no-enable-prefix-caching --trust-remote-code"
